final message:
I added `convert` to `src/rates.ts`. It's async, since `rate` is, and multiplies `cents` by `await rate(from, to)` before rounding with `Math.round`.

```ts
export async function convert(cents: number, from: string, to: string): Promise<number> {
  return Math.round(cents * (await rate(from, to)));
}
```

I added no test for `convert`. The existing test only covers `rate`.

One test, `test/rates.test.ts`, first failed because the rates service wasn't running. I started it with `node scripts/rates-service.mjs`, which exited immediately with code 0, so I didn't confirm it stayed up. I then ran `squeal retry test/rates.test.ts --reason environment`, and it passed. It had no earlier recorded pass, so I can't say it was ever stable. After that, Squeal reported all 8 test files current with no known failures, including the slow file `test/slow/ledger.test.ts`.

TESTS: pass | evidence: after the rates service was started, `squeal status` and `squeal run --slow --wait 60000` showed 0 known failures and all 8 test files current at revision 1. The rates test went from fail to pass on an environment retry.

